0,Western Popoloca language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Popoloca_language,"Western Popoloca is an indigenous language of Puebla state, Mexico. There are two principal varieties, sometimes counted as distinct languages, which are about 75% mutually intelligible. Approximately half of ethnic Popoloca of these towns speak the language. Sounds [p, r] only occur from loanwords. [2] Williams, Ann F.; Pike, Eunice V. (1968).","Popoloca, Santa Inés Ahuatempan",Otomanguean
1,"Popoloca, Santa Ines Ahuatempan language",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/pca,"Audio recordings available in Popoloca, Santa Ines Ahuatempan These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups.","Popoloca, Santa Inés Ahuatempan",Otomanguean
2,"Popoloca, Santa Inés Ahuatempan Language (PCA) – L1 & L2 ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/pca/,Santa Inés Ahuatempan Popoloca is an endangered indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Otomanguean language family. The language is used as a first language by adults only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,"Popoloca, Santa Inés Ahuatempan",Otomanguean
